Mathematically, if you have $1.2M in cash and a net burn rate of $62K/month, your runway should be roughly 19 months ($1.2M / $62K). If your internal projection is only a 6-month runway, your audience (board, executives, or investors) will immediately ask why. 
*   **The Fix:** Ensure your narrative clearly explains this gap. Are there large upcoming capital expenditures, debt repayments, planned hiring surges, or seasonal revenue dips that compress the runway to 6 months? Make sure this is explicitly stated so the math makes sense to your audience.

**2. Margin Improvement Strategy**
